# oracle: fix wall/ees (cut down from examples/PACKAGES/ees/in.fix_wall, Data_wall): six ellipsoids near the zlo and zhi
# walls (sigman, the ellipsoid half-length along the normal, is below the wall distance for all but the closest one);
# the wall force and the torque on each ellipsoid, and the energy and per-wall force sums.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
# measured with native LAMMPS: max relative error below 1e-13 (per-atom and thermo)
# oracle-inputs: w133mf_wall_ees.data
# native: b332f28 built with the installed lmp (EXTRA-FIX)
units lj
atom_style ellipsoid
boundary p p f
read_data w133mf_wall_ees.data
pair_style zero 1.0
pair_coeff * *
timestep 0.0002
compute temp all temp/asphere
thermo_modify temp temp
fix EES_substrate all wall/ees zhi EDGE 10 1 10 zlo EDGE 10 1 10
fix NVE all nve/asphere
thermo_style custom step temp press etotal f_EES_substrate f_EES_substrate[1] f_EES_substrate[2]
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 50
run 200
